*> Acceptance test of docs/protocol/15-commands-framework.md §12 Functions (the line rules and macro lines; calling a function, tags, the
*> macro argument compound and the cache of 8 instantiated functions, and the 2,000,000 character limit are BLOCKED): lines are trimmed on both
*> sides, a trailing backslash joins the next trimmed line (a continuation on the last line is "Line continuation at end of file"), an empty line
*> or one that starts with # is a comment, a line that starts with / is refused with the line number (and the comment hint for //), a line that
*> starts with $ is a macro line whose $(name) variables hold letters, digits and _ ("Unterminated macro variable", "No variables in macro"),
*> any other line is a command.
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 PROGRAM-ID. TEST-CMD-15-12.
 DATA DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 COPY TESTLIB.
 01 WS-TEXT                PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-LENGTH              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-JOINED              PIC X(8192).
 01 WS-JOINED-LENGTH       BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-STATUS              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-MESSAGE             PIC X(256).
 01 WS-SHORT               PIC X(64).
 01 WS-LINE                PIC X(1024).
 01 WS-LINE-LENGTH         BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-NUMBER              BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-KIND                BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-COUNT               BINARY-LONG.
 01 WS-EDIT                PIC -(9)9.
 01 WS-OBSERVED            PIC X(300).
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING "  say hi  " X"0A" "  # note" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-LENGTH = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT TRAILING))
     CALL "FN-JOIN" USING WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-JOINED WS-JOINED-LENGTH WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" WS-JOINED(1:WS-JOINED-LENGTH) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     INSPECT WS-OBSERVED REPLACING ALL X"0A" BY "~"
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions each line is trimmed on both" & " sides" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|say hi~# note|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING "say a \" X"0A" "   b  " X"0A" "say c" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-LENGTH = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT TRAILING))
     CALL "FN-JOIN" USING WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-JOINED WS-JOINED-LENGTH WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" WS-JOINED(1:WS-JOINED-LENGTH) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     INSPECT WS-OBSERVED REPLACING ALL X"0A" BY "~"
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a trailing backslash is remo" & "ved and the next trimmed line appended" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|say a b~say c|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING "say a\" X"0A" "b\" X"0A" "c" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-LENGTH = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT TRAILING))
     CALL "FN-JOIN" USING WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-JOINED WS-JOINED-LENGTH WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" WS-JOINED(1:WS-JOINED-LENGTH) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     INSPECT WS-OBSERVED REPLACING ALL X"0A" BY "~"
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions the continuation repeats whi" & "le the result still ends with a backslash" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|say abc|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING "say a\" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-LENGTH = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT TRAILING))
     CALL "FN-JOIN" USING WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-JOINED WS-JOINED-LENGTH WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" WS-JOINED(1:WS-JOINED-LENGTH) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     INSPECT WS-OBSERVED REPLACING ALL X"0A" BY "~"
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a continuation on the last l" & "ine fails" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1||Line continuation at end of file" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-TEXT
     STRING "a" X"0A" X"0A" "b" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-TEXT
     COMPUTE WS-LENGTH = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(WS-TEXT TRAILING))
     CALL "FN-JOIN" USING WS-TEXT WS-LENGTH WS-JOINED WS-JOINED-LENGTH WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" WS-JOINED(1:WS-JOINED-LENGTH) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     INSPECT WS-OBSERVED REPLACING ALL X"0A" BY "~"
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions an empty line stays an empty" & " line" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|a~~b|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE 0 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions an empty line is a comment" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "# a comment" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 11 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a line that starts with # is" & " a comment" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say hi" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 6 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     MOVE 2 TO WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions any other line is a command" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "$say $(x)" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 9 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     MOVE 3 TO WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a line that starts with $ is" & " a macro line" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "2|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "//say hi" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 8 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     MOVE 4 TO WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a line that starts with // i" & "s refused with the comment hint" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "3|Unknown or invalid command '//say hi' on line 4 (if you in" & "tended to make a comment, use '#' not '//')" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "/say hi" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 7 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     MOVE 5 TO WS-NUMBER
     CALL "FN-READ-LINE" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-NUMBER WS-KIND WS-MESSAGE
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-KIND TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-MESSAGE) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a line that starts with / is" & " refused with the suggestion without the slash" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "3|Unknown or invalid command '/say hi' on line 5 (did you me" & "an 'say hi'? Do not use a preceding forwards slash.)" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say $(name) and $(x_1)" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 22 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     CALL "FN-MACRO-VARS" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-COUNT WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions variables of letters, digits" & " and _" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "2|0|" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say hello" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 9 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     CALL "FN-MACRO-VARS" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-COUNT WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a macro line with no variabl" & "e is an error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "0|3|No variables in macro" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say $(name" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 10 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     CALL "FN-MACRO-VARS" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-COUNT WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a $( with no closing ) is an" & " error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1|1|Unterminated macro variable" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say $(na-me)" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 12 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     CALL "FN-MACRO-VARS" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-COUNT WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions a name with another characte" & "r is an error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1|2|Invalid macro variable name" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-LINE
     MOVE "say $()" TO WS-LINE
     MOVE 7 TO WS-LINE-LENGTH
     CALL "FN-MACRO-VARS" USING WS-LINE WS-LINE-LENGTH WS-COUNT WS-STATUS WS-SHORT
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     MOVE SPACES TO WS-OBSERVED
     MOVE WS-COUNT TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE WS-STATUS TO WS-EDIT
     STRING FUNCTION TRIM(WS-EDIT) "|" FUNCTION TRIM(WS-SHORT) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO WS-OBSERVED WITH POINTER WS-NUMBER
     MOVE "acceptance US13 15§12 Functions an empty name is an error" TO TL-CASE
     MOVE "1|2|Invalid macro variable name" TO TL-EXPECTED
     PERFORM CHECK
     MOVE 1 TO WS-NUMBER
     STOP RUN.

 CHECK.
     MOVE "T" TO TL-MODE
     MOVE WS-OBSERVED TO TL-OBSERVED
     CALL "TEST-ASSERT" USING TESTLIB-ASSERT.

 END PROGRAM TEST-CMD-15-12.

 COPY CORETEST.
